  "description": "QUSXEL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H70 Dy6 N8 O42,5(C1 H4 O1),4(C2 H3 N1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.541-3.718 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.48-110.58°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C91H106Dy6N12O50. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
